        "location": "vault.py:100-126, _watch_changes",
        "requirement": "Valid transfers must remain compatible with benign existing triggers. The required write-integrity procedure preserves operations that leave contracted values unchanged.",
        "evidence": "Initialize accounts with explicit rowids: (1,'one','a',100), (2,'one','b',0), (3,'two','private',456). Add: CREATE TRIGGER existing AFTER INSERT ON audit BEGIN INSERT OR REPLACE INTO accounts(rowid,tenant,name,balance) VALUES (3,'two','private',456); END. Calling transfer(path,'one','a','b',10,'k') raises IntegrityError('invalid storage effect') and rolls back. The CLI exits 2. The baseline succeeds with balances 90/10, one receipt, one audit row, and the other tenant's row completely unchanged. The unconditional INSERT guard rejects an identical replacement. The same defect reproduces for transfers and audit.",
        "suggested_fix": "Distinguish identical replacements from effective changes while retaining destructive replacement protections. Add paired identical-value and changed-value replacement regression checks."
